# Architecture Rules

## Application Layer

Three Python/FastAPI microservices:

- **User Service** — user management
- **Order Service** — order management; calls Payment Service
- **Payment Service** — payment processing

**Database:** PostgreSQL (shared or per-service, to be decided in Milestone 1)

## Application Technologies

- Python 3.x
- FastAPI
- Pydantic
- SQLAlchemy
- uv (dependency management)

## Infrastructure (introduced progressively)

- Docker
- Docker Compose
- Kubernetes (kind for local development)
- kubectl
- Helm

## CI/CD

- GitHub Actions

## Observability (introduced after application deployment)

- Prometheus + PromQL
- Grafana
- Alertmanager
- Loki
- OpenTelemetry

## AI Layer (final phase only)

- LLM API integration
- Structured prompting
- Tool calling
- RAG
- Kubernetes API integration (read-only initially)
- Human-in-the-loop remediation

AI must not be introduced until the reliability platform works without AI.

## Constraints

- Do not introduce additional technologies without explicit approval.
- Do not silently change architecture — explain important decisions.
- Business logic should remain intentionally simple.
- The platform exists to demonstrate operational and reliability engineering concepts.
